The '''2023–24 South African Premiership''', known as the '''DSTV Premiership''' for sponsorship reasons, and also commonly referred to as the [[Premier Soccer League|PSL]] after the governing body, was the 28th consecutive season of the [[South African Premiership]]. The season ran from 4 August 2023 and concluded on 25 May 2024. [[Mamelodi Sundowns F.C.|Mamelodi Sundowns]] successfully defended the title with 6 games remaining, winning the title for the seventh consecutive year, starting  from the [[2017–18 South African Premier Division|2017–18]] season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.psl.co.za/news/article/5606844-sundowns-thump-chiefs-to-secure-seven|title=Official South African Premier Soccer League page|date=2 May 2024}}</ref>

[[Kaizer Chiefs F.C.|Kaizer Chiefs]], who've won the title four times, finished tenth, their lowest ever finish in the [[Premier Soccer League|PSL]] era.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Chiefs lose at Spurs for worst-ever league finish |url=https://supersport.com/football/dstv-premiership/news/bb661d65-53c8-4cc1-829c-88a26f68e7a2/chiefs-lose-at-spurs-for-worst-ever-league-finish |access-date=2024-07-03 |website=SuperSport |language=en}}</ref>

